---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MediaHeader from '../components/MediaHeader.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { PAGE_SEO, PRACTICE, DOCTOR } from '../consts';
import { UAN_HREF } from '../lib/practice-links';

const trail = [{ name: 'Terms & medical disclaimer', href: '/terms' }];
const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={PAGE_SEO.terms.title}
  description={PAGE_SEO.terms.description}
  breadcrumbs={trail}
>
  <MediaHeader
    trail={trail}
    title="Terms and medical"
    titleEm="disclaimer"
    size="md"
    lede={`The terms governing use of this website, and the status of the health information published on it. Last updated ${updated}.`}
  />

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;" aria-label="Terms of use and medical disclaimer">
    <div class="container terms">
      {/* The emergency notice goes first, before any of the terms. It is the
          only thing on this page a person in trouble needs, and burying it under
          eight numbered clauses would be a drafting decision with a cost. */}
      <aside class="callout" data-reveal>
        <span class="callout__icon"><Icon name="pulse" size="sm" /></span>
        <div>
          <p class="callout__title">This website is not for emergencies</p>
          <p>
            If you or someone else is at immediate risk of harm, do not use this website.
            Go to the emergency department at {PRACTICE.affiliation}, or call the hospital
            directly. <a href={UAN_HREF}>Hospital UAN {PRACTICE.hospitalUan}</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <div class="rich" data-reveal-group>
        <h2 data-reveal>1. Medical disclaimer</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          Everything published on this website is general health information. It describes
          conditions, symptoms and treatments in the way a good leaflet would, and it is
          written to help you decide whether to seek an assessment.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal>
          It is <strong>not</strong> medical advice about you, and reading it does not create
          a doctor–patient relationship. A diagnosis depends on your history, your
          examination, your physical health and your circumstances, none of which a web page
          has access to. Several of the conditions described here share symptoms with each
          other and with physical illnesses that need entirely different treatment. Telling
          them apart is what a consultation is for.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal>
          Do not use this site to diagnose yourself, to diagnose someone else, or to start,
          change or stop any medication. Stopping a psychiatric medication abruptly can be
          harmful, and it should only be done under supervision.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>2. Accuracy and currency</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          The clinical content is written to reflect current, mainstream psychiatric
          practice, and care is taken to keep it accurate. Medicine changes, however, and no
          guarantee is given that every page reflects the most recent evidence at the moment
          you read it. Where this site and your treating clinician disagree, follow your
          clinician.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal>
          Clinic hours, fees and contact details are published in good faith but are set by
          {PRACTICE.affiliation} and can change without notice. Please confirm them by
          telephone before travelling.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>3. Appointments and fees</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          This website does not take bookings. Appointments are arranged through
          {PRACTICE.affiliation}, and consultation fees, payment methods and any accepted
          health plans are set by the hospital rather than here. Nothing on this site
          constitutes an offer of treatment or a guarantee of availability.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>4. No guarantee of outcome</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          Psychiatric treatment is effective for most people, and this site says so. It does
          not promise a particular result for you. Response to treatment varies between
          individuals, timelines given on these pages are typical rather than certain, and no
          statement here should be read as a guarantee of recovery.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>5. Links to other websites</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          This site links to {PRACTICE.affiliation} and to Dr. Qazi's consultant profile
          there. Those sites are controlled by others, and no responsibility is taken for
          their content, their accuracy or their privacy practices.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>6. Copyright</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          The text, design and code of this website belong to {DOCTOR.name} and may not be
          reproduced or republished without permission. Photographs used on the site are
          licensed stock images and remain the property of their respective creators. You
          are welcome to link to any page here, and to print pages for your own use or to
          discuss with your family.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>7. Testimonials and reviews</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          No patient testimonial appears on this site unless it is genuine and published with
          the written consent of the person who gave it. No patient is identified anywhere on
          this website.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          To the extent permitted by law, no liability is accepted for any loss or harm
          arising from reliance on the general information published here. Use of this site
          is at your own discretion, and it is not a substitute for an individual
          consultation with a qualified clinician.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>9. Governing law</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Islamic Republic of Pakistan, and any
          dispute arising from them falls to the courts of Peshawar, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>10. Contact</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          Questions about these terms can be sent to
          <a href={`mailto:${PRACTICE.email}`}>{PRACTICE.email}</a>, or raised at your
          appointment. For anything clinical, please
          <a href="/contact">book a consultation</a> rather than writing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .terms .callout { margin-bottom: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); }
</style>
